$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure A mixture of
hexane-2,5-dione (684 mg, 6 mmol), aniline (465 mg, 5 mmol), and Pr(OTf)3
(294mg, 10mol%) was stirred at room temperature under solvent-free
conditions for 2 h. After completion of the reaction, as indicated by
thin layer chromotography (TLC), the reaction mixture was diluted with
ethyl acetate. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4),
and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (15% ethyl acetate in hexane) to afford the pure product
(735 mg) in 86% yield. All compounds are known and were identified by
comparison with those of the authentic samples.[9-15] 2h, yield 81%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
