$DATUM 52093-27-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure A mixture of hexane-2,5-dione (684 mg, 6 mmol), aniline
(465 mg, 5 mmol), and Pr(OTf)3 (294mg, 10mol%) was stirred at room
temperature under solvent-free conditions for 2 h. After completion of
the reaction, as indicated by thin layer chromotography (TLC), the
reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The residue
was purified by silica-gel column chromatography (15% ethyl acetate in
hexane) to afford the pure product (735 mg) in 86% yield. All compounds
are known and were identified by comparison with those of the authentic
samples.[9-15] 2,5-Dimethyl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrrole (2a, entry 1):Oil, yield
735 mg 86%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.06 (s, 6 H), 5.94 (s, 2 H),
7.20-7.28 (m, 2 H), 7.42-7.54 (m, 3 H). HRMS calcd. for C12H13N:
171.1048; found. 171.1049. Anal. calcd. for C12H13N: C, 84.17; H, 7.65;
N, 8.18. Found: C, 84.19; H, 7.71; N,8.21.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple Synthesis of Pyrroles Under Solvent-Free Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM De, Surya K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2008), 38(16), 2768-2774

