$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis and characterization of
polysubstitued furans To a dry Schlenk tube that charged with nitrogen,
1,4-dione 4 (0.2 mmol) was added, then freshly distilled CH3CN (2.0 mL)
was injected through a syringe. Subsequently, TfOH (17.3 μL, 0.2 mmol)
was added to the mixture, and the resulting solution was stirred at 85 °C
for 1 h. Then the resulting solution was cooled to room temperature, and
solvent was evaporated under vacuum, the residue was purified by flash
column chromatography on silica gel (eluent: ethyl acetate/ petroleum
ether). The furan 5 Ethyl 2,5-diphenylfuran-3-carboxylate (5b): 13b
Isolated by flash column chromatography (ethyl acetate/petroleum ether =
1:10) in 80% yield. Yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 8.10 (d, J =
8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.76 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.50-7.41 (m, 5H), 7.33 (t, J =
7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.11 (s, 1H), 4.35 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.38 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
3H),; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 163.5, 156.4, 152.3, 129.7, 129.3,
128.7, 128.3, 128.1, 128.0, 123.9, 115.7, 107.9, 60.6, 14.2. Rf = 0.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr furan synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Rearrangement of tert-Butylperoxides for the Construction of
Polysubstituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zheng, Xiaojian; Lu, Shenglin; Li, Zhiping
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(21), 5432-5435

