$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 107-06-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of trisubstituted furans 5a-v To a
flame-dried schlenk tube were added phosphorane 1 (0.25 mmol, 1.0 eq) and
symmetric 1,2-diketone 3 (0.25 mmol, 1.0 equiv). The tube was vacuumized
and back-filled with N2, followed by the addition of 1.0 mL of anhydrous
toluene. The resulting mixture was stirred at 120 °C for the time
indicated in table 2 till almost full conversion of 1 by TLC analysis.
After cooling to room temperature, the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure and 1.0 mL of anhydrous ClCH2CH2Cl was added. Then HSiCl3 (58
mg, 45 uL, 0.5 mmol) was added in one portion and the reaction mixture
was stirred vigorously. After the full conversion of the intermediate I
by TLC analysis, two drops of MeOH was added into the resulting mixture
and further vigorously stirring was needed to promote the transformation
of the intermediate 1,4-diketone III to the furan product. Then the
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was directly
subjected to flash column chromatograph using petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate as the eluent. The desired product 5a-x. Column chromatography
afforded the desired product 5a 14 in 84% yield (62.6 mg) as white solid.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.78-7.76 (m, 2H), 7.62-7.60 (m, 2H),
7.48-7.46 (m, 2H), 7.44-7.37 (m, 4H), 7.35-7.23 (m, 5H), 6.82 (s, 1H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 152.58, 147.92, 134.35, 131.14, 130.56,
128.78, 128.45, 128.42, 127.54, 127.32, 126.17, 126.14, 124.56, 123.85,
109.50.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-waste reduction, one-pot Wittig/1,4-reduction/Paal-Knorr
sequence, Ph3PO generated in stage 1 and HCl generated in stage 3 acting
as catalysts, screw capped pressure tube used, toluene removed after
stage 1, optimization study (based on solvents, temperature and work up)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Successively Recycle Waste as Catalyst: A One-Pot
Wittig/1,4-Reduction/Paal-Knorr Sequence for Modular Synthesis of
Substituted Furans
