$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
trisubstituted furans 5a-v To a flame-dried schlenk tube were added
phosphorane 1 (0.25 mmol, 1.0 eq) and symmetric 1,2-diketone 3 (0.25
mmol, 1.0 equiv). The tube was vacuumized and back-filled with N2,
followed by the addition of 1.0 mL of anhydrous toluene. The resulting
mixture was stirred at 120 °C for the time indicated in table 2 till
almost full conversion of 1 by TLC analysis. After cooling to room
temperature, the solvent was removed under reduced pressure and 1.0 mL of
anhydrous ClCH2CH2Cl was added. Then HSiCl3 (58 mg, 45 uL, 0.5 mmol) was
added in one portion and the reaction mixture was stirred vigorously.
After the full conversion of the intermediate I by TLC analysis, two
drops of MeOH was added into the resulting mixture and further vigorously
stirring was needed to promote the transformation of the intermediate
1,4-diketone III to the furan product. Then the solvent was removed under
reduced pressure, and the residue was directly subjected to flash column
chromatograph using petroleum ether/ethyl acetate as the eluent. The
desired product 5a-x. Column chromatography afforded the desired product
5b 14 in 80% yield (64.8 mg) as white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.65 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.42 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 7.41-7.25 (m, 4H),
7.18-7.11 (m, 1H), 7.08 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.02 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H),
6.68 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 2.24 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 152.10, 147.93, 137.26, 136.84, 131.36, 130.62, 129.31, 129.06,
128.66, 128.47, 128.42, 127.30, 126.05, 123.76, 123.68, 109.39, 21.29,
21.23.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-waste reduction, one-pot Wittig/1,4-reduction/Paal-Knorr
sequence, Ph3PO generated in stage 1 and HCl generated in stage 3 acting
as catalysts, screw capped pressure tube used, toluene removed after
stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Successively Recycle Waste as Catalyst: A One-Pot
Wittig/1,4-Reduction/Paal-Knorr Sequence for Modular Synthesis of
Substituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
